    "q-95642": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95642",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
