    "q-95263": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95263",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=9\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=9\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95263-a",
