    "q-95649": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95649",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
