    "q-95648": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95648",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int (2x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
