    "q-95655": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95655",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5(1-{x}^{2})}+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x$ for $|x|<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5(1-{x}^{2})}+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
