    "q-95659": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95659",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int (\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4(1-{x}^{2})}+4x)\\text{d}x$  for $|x|<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4(1-{x}^{2})}+4x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
